1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,292
If you smoke meat, the dead can smell your dinner.

2
00:00:04,030 --> 00:00:08,472
The Harvest. Part three of three. The cold smokehouse.

3
00:00:09,072 --> 00:00:11,081
Smoke keeps meat for months.

4
00:00:11,381 --> 00:00:14,019
And calls the dead for miles.

5
00:00:14,619 --> 00:00:19,763
Salt it. Dry it. Keep it cool and dark. No fire. No smoke.

6
00:00:20,363 --> 00:00:22,193
I will taste-test everything.

7
00:00:22,493 --> 00:00:24,858
If it smells wrong, it is wrong.

8
00:00:26,123 --> 00:00:30,620
A bulging jar, a bad smell, any doubt: throw it out.

9
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:34,595
A cellar a meter and a half down stays cool all winter.

10
00:00:35,720 --> 00:00:38,664
Nineteen days became sixty-four.

11
00:00:40,220 --> 00:00:41,448
We will make it to spring.

12
00:00:41,748 --> 00:00:43,562
If you stop eating the seeds.

13
00:00:45,260 --> 00:00:48,851
Winter arrives. And a radio crackles in the barn.

14
00:00:49,451 --> 00:00:55,345
The Harvest. Part three of three. Follow for the next story.
